EAST BAY FOUNDERS WEEKLY
Friday, March 6, 2026

Hi all. What's happening for founders in Oakland, Berkeley, Emeryville and Alameda this week.

DEMO NIGHT RECAP
Seventy-nine people, six companies, one projector failure handled gracefully by a founder who demoed from a laptop held over her head. The houseplant app got the loudest applause; the plant-floor robotics team got the most follow-up conversations. Photos in the portal. Thank you to everyone who presented and to the roaster downstairs for staying open.

COMING UP
- Founder Breakfast, Friday March 20, 8:00am, Temescal. Informal, no agenda, coffee and pastries, 25 people max. RSVP in the portal.
- Uptown coworking opens March 16; the member discount is live in the portal.
- A members-only session on state payroll tax changes with a local CPA, Tuesday March 17, noon, online. Boring and useful.

NEWS
Two of our members are on the speaker list for the Pacific Plant Automation Expo in San Jose next week. If you are going, the member meetup is Thursday evening at the hotel bar; reply for details.

The Alameda office-share request from last week found a match. This is the newsletter working as intended.

MEMBER NEWS
- A member's climate fintech announced a seed round. Congratulations.
- A hardware member is looking for a contract firmware engineer for six weeks; posting on the job board.
- Someone left a very nice jacket at Demo Night. It is at the space.

JOB BOARD: 17 open roles. https://eastbayfounders.org/jobs

Have a good weekend.

